<!DOCTYPE Bill PUBLIC "-//LSC//DTD Authoring Bill XML//EN" "l:\dtd\author\billauthoring.top"><Bill version="1.0" type="introLN"><IntroducedBillHeader><RequestNumber>Z-0779.2</RequestNumber><BillNumber>HOUSE BILL 2559</BillNumber><StateLegSession><State>State of Washington</State><Legislature>59th Legislature</Legislature><Session>2006 Regular Session</Session></StateLegSession><Sponsors>Representatives Hasegawa, Pettigrew and Linville; by request of Department of Agriculture</Sponsors><IntroHistory><ReadDate>Read first time 01/10/2006.  </ReadDate><ReferredTo>Referred to Committee on Economic Development, Agriculture &amp; Trade.</ReferredTo></IntroHistory></IntroducedBillHeader><BriefDescription>Changing the registration fees for weighing and measuring devices.</BriefDescription><BillBody><BillTitle><LineNumber line=" 1" page="1,1" hrt="no"/>	AN ACT Relating to registration fees for weighing and measuring<LineNumber line=" 2" page="1,2"/>devices; amending RCW 19.94.175; and providing an effective date.</BillTitle><EnactingClause><LineNumber line=" 3" page="1,3" hrt="no"/>BE IT ENACTED BY THE LEGISLATURE OF THE STATE OF WASHINGTON:</EnactingClause><BillSection type="amend"><LineNumber line=" 4" page="1,4" hrt="no"/><BegSecAmd><SecNum>Sec. </SecNum><BegSecText>RCW <Cite>19.94.175</Cite> and 1995 c 355 s 7 are each amended to read<LineNumber line=" 5" page="1,5"/>as follows:</BegSecText><LineNumber line=" 6" page="1,6" hrt="no"/></BegSecAmd><RCWSLText>	(1) Pursuant to RCW 19.94.015, the following annual registration<LineNumber line=" 7" page="1,7"/>fees shall be charged for each weighing or measuring instrument or<LineNumber line=" 8" page="1,8"/>device used for commercial purposes in this state:<paraend/><paraendLessSpace/><tblwrap format="narrow10ln" rowmargins="zerotopbottom"><table frame="none"><tgroup cols="5" colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left"><colspec colname="1" colwidth="155pt"/><colspec colname="2" colwidth="31pt"/><colspec colname="3" colwidth="135pt"/><colspec colname="4" colwidth="22pt"/><colspec colname="5" colwidth="54pt"/><tbody valign="top"><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line=" 9" page="1,9" hrt="no"/></entry><entry align="right">(a)</entry><entry namest="3" nameend="5" align="justify">Weighing devices:</entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line="10" page="1,10" hrt="no"/><LineNumber line="11" page="1,11"/></entry><entry align="right">(i)</entry><entry align="justify">Small scales &quot;zero to four<paraend addedByLN="yes"/>hundred pounds capacity&quot;<hardspace/><DotsRight/></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">$</entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">((<strike>5.00</strike>))<paraend/><add>12.50</add></entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line="12" page="1,12" hrt="no"/><LineNumber line="13" page="1,13"/><LineNumber line="14" page="1,14"/></entry><entry align="right">(ii)</entry><entry align="justify">Intermediate scales &quot;four<paraend addedByLN="yes"/>hundred one pounds to five<paraend addedByLN="yes"/>thousand pounds capacity&quot;<hardspace/><DotsRight/></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">$</entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">((<strike>20.00</strike>))<paraend/><add>50.00</add></entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line="15" page="1,15" hrt="no"/><LineNumber line="16" page="1,16"/></entry><entry align="right">(iii)</entry><entry align="justify">Large scales &quot;over five<paraend addedByLN="yes"/>thousand pounds capacity&quot;<hardspace/><DotsRight/></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">$</entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">((<strike>52.00</strike>))<paraend/><add>130.00</add></entry></row><PageNumberFooter>		p. 1	HB 2559</PageNumberFooter><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line=" 1" page="2,1" hrt="no"/><LineNumber line=" 2" page="2,2"/><LineNumber line=" 3" page="2,3"/></entry><entry align="right">(iv)</entry><entry align="justify">((<strike>Large scales with<paraend addedByLN="yes"/>supplemental<paraend/>devices<hardspace/><DotsRight/></strike></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right"><strike>$</strike></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right"><strike>52.00</strike></entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line=" 4" page="2,4" hrt="no"/><LineNumber line=" 5" page="2,5"/></entry><entry align="right"><strike>(v)</strike>))</entry><entry align="justify">Railroad track scales<hardspace/><DotsRight/></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">$</entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">((<strike>800.00</strike>))<paraend/><add>2,000.00</add></entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line=" 6" page="2,6" hrt="no"/></entry><entry align="right">(b)</entry><entry namest="3" nameend="5" align="justify">Liquid fuel metering devices:</entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line=" 7" page="2,7" hrt="no"/><LineNumber line=" 8" page="2,8"/><LineNumber line=" 9" page="2,9"/></entry><entry align="right">(i)</entry><entry align="justify">Motor fuel meters with flows of<paraend addedByLN="yes"/>((<strike>less than</strike>)) twenty gallons <add>or<paraend addedByLN="yes"/>less</add> per minute<hardspace/><DotsRight/></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">$</entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">((<strike>5.00</strike>))<paraend/><add>12.50</add></entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line="10" page="2,10" hrt="no"/><LineNumber line="11" page="2,11"/><LineNumber line="12" page="2,12"/><LineNumber line="13" page="2,13"/></entry><entry align="right">(ii)</entry><entry align="justify">Motor fuel meters with flows of<paraend addedByLN="yes"/>more than twenty but not more<paraend addedByLN="yes"/>than one hundred fifty gallons<paraend addedByLN="yes"/>per minute<hardspace/><DotsRight/></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">$</entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">((<strike>16.00</strike>))<paraend/><add>40.00</add></entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line="14" page="2,14" hrt="no"/><LineNumber line="15" page="2,15"/><LineNumber line="16" page="2,16"/></entry><entry align="right">(iii)</entry><entry align="justify">Motor fuel meters with flows<paraend addedByLN="yes"/>over one hundred fifty gallons<paraend addedByLN="yes"/>per minute<hardspace/><DotsRight/></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">$</entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">((<strike>25.00</strike>))<paraend/><add>62.50</add></entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line="17" page="2,17" hrt="no"/></entry><entry align="right">(c)</entry><entry namest="3" nameend="5" align="justify">Liquid petroleum gas meters:</entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line="18" page="2,18" hrt="no"/><LineNumber line="19" page="2,19"/></entry><entry align="right">(i)</entry><entry align="justify">With one inch diameter or<paraend addedByLN="yes"/>smaller dispensers<hardspace/><DotsRight/></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">$</entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">((<strike>10.00</strike>))<paraend/><add>25.00</add></entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line="20" page="2,20" hrt="no"/><LineNumber line="21" page="2,21"/></entry><entry align="right">(ii)</entry><entry align="justify">With greater than one inch<paraend addedByLN="yes"/>diameter dispensers<hardspace/><DotsRight/></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">$</entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">((<strike>30.00</strike>))<paraend/><add>75.00</add></entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line="22" page="2,22" hrt="no"/><LineNumber line="23" page="2,23"/></entry><entry align="right">(d)</entry><entry align="justify">Fabric meters<hardspace/><DotsRight/></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">$</entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">((<strike>5.00</strike>))<paraend/><add>12.50</add></entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line="24" page="2,24" hrt="no"/><LineNumber line="25" page="2,25"/></entry><entry align="right">(e)</entry><entry align="justify">Cordage meters<hardspace/><DotsRight/></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">$</entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">((<strike>5.00</strike>))<paraend/><add>12.50</add></entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line="26" page="2,26" hrt="no"/><LineNumber line="27" page="2,27"/></entry><entry align="right">(f)</entry><entry align="justify">Mass flow meters<hardspace/><DotsRight/></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">$</entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">((<strike>14.00</strike>))<paraend/><add>35.00</add></entry></row><row><entry colsep="0" rowsep="0" align="left" forln="yes"><LineNumber line="28" page="2,28" hrt="no"/><LineNumber line="29" page="2,29"/></entry><entry align="right">(g)</entry><entry align="justify">Taxi meters<hardspace/><DotsRight/></entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">$</entry><entry valign="bottom" align="right">((<strike>5.00</strike>))<paraend/><add>12.50</add></entry></row></tbody></tgroup></table><paraendLessSpace/></tblwrap><LineNumber line="30" page="2,30"/>	(2) With the exception of subsection (3) of this section, no person<LineNumber line="31" page="2,31"/>shall be required to pay more than the ((<strike>established</strike>)) <add>annual</add><LineNumber line="32" page="2,32"/><add>registration</add> fee ((<strike>adopted under this section</strike>)) for any weighing or<LineNumber line="33" page="2,33"/>measuring instrument or device in any one year.<paraend/><LineNumber line="34" page="2,34" hrt="no"/>	(3) The department or a city sealer may establish reasonable<LineNumber line="35" page="2,35"/>inspection and testing fees for each type or class of weighing or<LineNumber line="36" page="2,36"/>measuring instrument or device specially requested to be inspected or<LineNumber line="37" page="2,37"/>tested by the device owner.  These inspection and testing fees shall be<LineNumber line="38" page="2,38"/>limited to those amounts necessary for the department or city sealer to<PageNumberFooter>	HB 2559	p. 2	</PageNumberFooter><LineNumber line=" 1" page="3,1" hrt="no"/>cover the direct costs associated with such inspection and testing.<endofsentence/><LineNumber line=" 2" page="3,2"/>The fees ((<strike>established under this subsection</strike>)) shall not be set so as<LineNumber line=" 3" page="3,3"/>to compete with service agents normally engaged in such services.</RCWSLText></BillSection><BillSection type="new" clausetype="effectivedate"><LineNumber line=" 4" page="3,4" hrt="no"/><BegSecNew><NewSecText>NEW SECTION.</NewSecText><SecNum>Sec. </SecNum></BegSecNew><RCWSLText>This act takes effect July 1, 2006.</RCWSLText></BillSection><BillEnd>--- END ---<PageNumberFooter lastpage="yes">		p. 3	HB 2559</PageNumberFooter></BillEnd></BillBody></Bill>